<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław III of Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1424–1444</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Vladislaus I of Hungary, Władysław Warneńczyk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1434 and, as Vladislaus I, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1440 until his death. His election in Hungary against the infant Ladislaus V led to civil war, but with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a> he waged the Long Campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1443–1444. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-varna">Battle of Varna</a> in 1444, earning the name Warneńczyk, 'of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a>'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland.jpg" alt="Władysław III of Poland" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_Warne%C5%84czyk_seal_1438_(cropped).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
